// Pull request author: elhoim
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Cloud Instance Metadata Credential Or Token Request Via CLI - Linux
// Sigma ID: 31f87cbb-010c-4dbc-8495-0b9f01a638de
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: elhoim
// Date: 2026-11-18 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1552.005
// Description: Detects a command line querying a cloud instance metadata service (IMDS) endpoint that returns
//   temporary credentials or access tokens of the role or managed identity attached to the instance.
//   Covers AWS EC2 IAM role credentials, the AWS ECS container credentials endpoint, Azure managed
//   identity tokens, GCP service account tokens and Alibaba Cloud RAM role credentials. Adversaries
//   with code execution on a cloud workload, or abusing an SSRF, query these endpoints to steal
//   credentials and pivot into the cloud control plane.
// False positives:
//   - Cloud bootstrap or configuration management scripts that read instance role credentials
//   - Administrators troubleshooting instance roles or managed identities
// References:
//   - https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/instance-metadata-security-credentials.html
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/managed-identities-azure-resources/how-to-use-vm-token
//   - https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/security-iam-roles.html
//   - https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/access/authenticate-workloads
//   - https://www.alibabacloud.com/help/en/ecs/user-guide/attach-an-instance-ram-role-to-an-ecs-instance
//   - https://hackingthe.cloud/aws/exploitation/ec2-metadata-ssrf/
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/388942adbd9641f4dfdcf079d7efe9a75ec0ac43/atomics/T1552.005/T1552.005.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/b0bbc60b952c72d5f6f518db6fefdfafc49584bc/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_cloud_imds_credential_request.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((ProcessCommandLine contains "100.100.100.200" or ProcessCommandLine contains "169.254.169.254" or ProcessCommandLine contains "169.254.170.2" or ProcessCommandLine contains "fd00:ec2::254" or ProcessCommandLine contains "metadata.google.internal") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/computeMetadata/v1/instance/service-accounts" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/meta-data/iam/security-credentials" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/meta-data/ram/security-credentials" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/metadata/identity/oauth2/token" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/v2/credentials")) and (not(((InitiatingProcessFolderPath in~ ("/usr/bin/amazon-ssm-agent", "/usr/bin/google_guest_agent", "/usr/bin/google_metadata_script_runner", "/usr/bin/ssm-agent-worker")) or InitiatingProcessFolderPath startswith "/snap/amazon-ssm-agent/")))
